<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Imran al-Fasi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1039</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Imran al-Fasi was a Moroccan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki</a> jurist who taught in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> in the early eleventh century. Around 1040 he persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudala">Gudala</a> chieftain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-ibn-ibrahim">Yahya ibn Ibrahim</a> to bring a religious teacher to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, which led to the arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-yasin">Abdallah ibn Yasin</a>. This encounter is treated as the genesis of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a>.</p></div>
